      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, but I'm worried the internal audit might still flag it as a bit lightweight on the technical specifics. Looking at the preliminary scan, the jargon score is decent, but we really need to push the density to the upper percentiles to be safe. \n\nCould you expand this section significantly? I need more depth on the molecular mechanisms, the specific kinetics, and the computational validation processes. Please try to maximize the technical nomenclature—I need that jargon score to be as high as possible so the reviewers don't question our rigor. Just make sure it still looks like a formal methodology.",
