    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "We administer a stemness-preserved electroporation (SE-PE) protocol using PfsZ-labeled Cas9–sgRNA RNP complexes conjugated to polyethylene glycol to enhance membrane permeabilization efficiency in primary HSCs. Following harsh damage accumulation, we execute single-molecule real-time investigation of chromosomal looping dynamics at the β-globin locus using next-generation sequencing (NGS) paired with CRISPR-Engage workflows for spatial mapping of DNA repair intermediates. Our bioinformatic pipeline leverages deep learning models trained on the DiVERGE and TargetScan databases to calculate percent identity thresholds, Chi-squared goodness-of-fit for off-target indel frequencies, and Bayesian posterior probability distributions to distinguish true variant signatures from background noise. Finally, we perform mass spectrometry-based proteomic profiling to quantify the retention of HAT1/HPF1 kinase activity post-modification, ensuring epigenetic reprogramming fidelity while modeling the kinetic half-life of the truncated RNP complex within the nuclear envelope.",
      "source": "target",
